{#if run?.bundleKind==='fixture'}<h2>sample data</h2><p>The public demo uses a gallery and forecasts made up from scratch. No real entrant titles, taglines or derived summaries are deployed. It demonstrates the interaction and deterministic pipeline, not real forecasting accuracy.</p><p>{run.gallery?.length} made-up projects; {run.points.length} made-up forecasts. Every card is labelled sample data.</p>{#if run.backtest}<p>Fixture coverage: {run.backtest.coverage.matched}/{run.backtest.eligible}. Fixture control: {run.backtest.control.matched}/{run.backtest.eligible}. Lift: {run.backtest.lift_pp} percentage points. Paired bootstrap interval: {run.backtest.ci_pp.join(' to ')} percentage points. These are fixture arithmetic, not real backtest findings.</p>{/if}<p>The fixture matcher compares authored audience, problem and mechanism tags. It is not an LLM judge and is never used to validate real gallery entries. The zero fixture gap is retained.</p><p>The sample layout is authored. Its vectors were produced with the actual shared BGE WASM embedding contract; density measures distances among these made-up sentences.</p>
{:else}<h2>Local recording build</h2><p>This build uses a locally retained model forecast. A real entrant backtest remains pending unless its validated run is explicitly provided. Model output is not an actual submission or a prediction timestamped before an event.</p>{/if}
<h2>Run provenance</h2>{#if run}<p>Run: <code>{run.runId}</code></p><p>Vector contract: <code>{run.contract.digest}</code></p><p>Attempts: {String(run.provenance?.attempted)}; valid points: {run.points.length}; failed samples: {String(run.provenance?.failures)}.</p>{/if}
<h2>Local-only real data</h2><p>The organizer ruling permits collection of the learn-ai.devpost.com gallery on this machine, with robots respected and at least three seconds between requests. Collected text, project URLs, SQLite prompts, per-project matches and recording bundles stay under ignored local directories. Only aggregate results may be public.</p><p>Permission to deploy anonymised, self-written summaries derived from the gallery has not been granted. The deployed demo therefore uses fixtures only. The local recording build is separate and must not be published.</p>
<h2>Placement and interview</h2><p>Personal placement runs on this device using BGE-small-en-v1.5, q8, CLS pooling and L2 normalization. Cosine distances in the original 384-dimensional space determine nearest neighbors and crowding. The mean distance to ten neighbors is ranked against the forecast's leave-one-out reference. Larger percentiles mean less crowded within that reference, not a better idea.</p><p>Questions come from traits shared by more than half the initial cluster and are capped at five. Answers, skips and Stop determine completion. Percentile never does. An answer does not prove avoidance; that requires your explicit confirmation.</p><h2>Privacy and recovery</h2><p>Your sentence and answers stay on your device. There is no personal inference server, account, analytics or cloud sync. Approximately 46 MB of hash-verified model/runtime assets come from the same site. Local browser storage preserves your own words and draft when available; Forget clears that record. Download the hand-off for a durable copy.</p><p>Changed run identities invalidate saved measurements. Words remain available, and re-placement is explicit. Measurements from different references are not compared.</p><h2>Scientific evidence</h2><p>No validated real coverage, control, lift or judge-reliability result exists in this checkout. The real backtest summary is marked not run. Source permission does not establish scientific validity. The frozen protocol separately requires matched budgets, a control, blind human labels, judge checks, uncertainty accounting and confidence intervals. No current Build With AI: Basics gallery is collected.</p><h2>Companion</h2><p>The organizer approved the installable companion. It retains the one-question-at-a-time interview and local hand-off, and writes nothing in devpost/ or Skill Pack files.</p><p>Runtime contract: <code>{contract.digest}</code>. Repository artifacts contain the fixture inputs, exact counts, configuration, manifests and reproduction instructions.</p></article><footer class="methods-footer"><span>Dark Space</span><a href="/">Return to the forecast map <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></footer></div>
